In a multi-provider set the invalid-type diagnostic anchors to the provider that
references the invalid type (Use, below), not the source-earliest provider of the
set (First). Missing is undefined; the loader tolerates the type error, and the
invalid type is buried in Use's interface-typed input.
-- config --
import-path: example.com/app
package-name: app
error-is: ErrInvalidType
-- example.com/app/a.go --
package app

type Thing struct{}
type Other struct{}

//plumb:build
func First() *Other { return &Other{} }

//plumb:build
func Use(r interface{ Read() Missing }) *Thing { return &Thing{} }
